{
  "source": "KingMinos OpenAPI resource inventory (public contract). Paths verified against live GET https://api.kingminos.com/openapi.json. Tool names are snake_case resource operationIds. Only operations whose effective security includes the bearer scheme are required MCP tools. This file is not application source.",
  "spec": "https://api.kingminos.com/openapi.yaml",
  "liveOpenApiJson": "https://api.kingminos.com/openapi.json",
  "exclusionPolicy": "Session/cookie routes under /v1/auth/* and /v1/account/* are permanently out of scope for MCP. MCP authenticates with a tenant Bearer; those routes are app/session surfaces (login, workspaces, members, invites, tokens). nonToolPathPrefixes is the durable deny-list; excludedOperationIds is the reviewed catalog of omitted operationIds. Excluding a route is a reviewed decision, not a silent skip. Do not add account/auth MCP tools.",
  "providersPolicy": "Pinned KingMinos OpenAPI provider enums for MCP Zod. CI fails when a pinned name is missing from ProviderName (routing.only) or CredentialProvider (put_credentials). Production OpenAPI may lag a merged BYOK provider (e.g. prospeo before the API Worker redeploys); npm run inventory:refresh unions live enums into this pin and never drops names. Live check (--live) is one-way: it fails only when the served spec lists a provider MCP Zod does not have.",
  "publicNonToolPaths": [
    "/health",
    "/openapi.yaml",
    "/v1/openapi.yaml",
    "/openapi.json",
    "/v1/openapi.json",
    "/api/v1/openapi.json"
  ],
  "nonToolPathPrefixes": ["/v1/auth", "/v1/account"],
